[{"code":"list_still_used","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":13,"col":27},"end":{"line":13,"col":43}},"title":"LIST CHANGED WHILE STILL IN USE","message":"`Set.insert` changes the set `old` in place, and another use still holds its\nstorage.\n\n12|                old = Set.singleton 1\n                   ^^^ this binding keeps the old storage\n13|                changed = Set.insert old 3\n                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the storage is changed here\n14|                Set.size old + Set.size changed\n                            ^^^ this use still needs the old storage\n\nChanging the slots or order would also change what the old set observes.\n\nMake an explicit storage copy with `Set.copy` before this write. Stored values\nremain shared; copy a stored value too if you need to change that value.\n\nTo keep the old storage unchanged, copy it at this use:\n\n13|                changed = Set.insert (Set.copy old) 3\n\nThis is sharing the code shows: old is read again at 14:17"}]
